@testray.main.component.name = "Patcher Builder"

Feature: Patcher Builder and 71 fixes
	Testing creation of 71 fixes on Patcher Builder.

Setup:
	* I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage

Scenario: Run fix pack builder agent job
	As a TSE, I should be able to run the fixpack-builder-agent job

	Given I start the fixpack-builder-agent job with the following parameters
	| osb.patcher.baseCommittish  | fix-pack-base-7110                                |
	| osb.patcher.committish      | LPS-89343_GA1                                     |
	| osb.patcher.fixIds          | 118757428                                         |
	| osb.patcher.gitRemoteURL    | git@github.com:CsabaTurcsan/liferay-portal-ee.git |
	| osb.patcher.patcherFixId    | 118757428                                         |
	| osb.patcher.productVersion  | DXP 7.1                                           |
	| osb.patcher.rebase          | false                                             |
	| osb.patcher.repository      | liferay-portal-ee                                 |
	| osb.patcher.type            | fix                                               |
	| patcher.fix.delivery.method | Fix Pack 3.0                                      |
	| patcher.request.key         | ff40197637bbd98565730e72f0ba6827091f7a77          |
	| patcher.user.id             | 72559402                                          |
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
	And I get the current build number for the job titled "fixpack-builder-agent(uat-test)"
	And I check the job with the name "fixpack-builder-agent(uat-test)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}" for completion
	And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
	Then the job with the name "fixpack-builder-agent(uat-test)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}" should have been successful